    not_duplicate_of: []  # f56b
    pr_ref:  # f56b
    description: "Dogfood validation of INV-ronuf on 2026-05-19 self-analysis verdicted **no_move** on the primary quantitative claim.\n\n**Pre-fix claim** (INV-ronuf description): 3 duplicate file-kind Symbols on self-analysis (ws-client.ts, test_websocket.py, serve.py), all emitted by websocket-linker-v1 in parallel with the language-side file Symbol.\n\n**PR #3805 closing entry's quantitative claim**: '3 → 0 phantom file Symbols on self-analysis'.\n\n**Post-fix self-analysis measurement** (verify script /tmp/inv-validation/verify_dogfood.py):\n- 3 file-kind Symbols with 'websocket' in origin (unchanged from pre-fix count)\n- 3 paths with duplicate file-kind Symbols:\n  - packages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts: origins={'javascript-v1', 'websocket-linker-v1'}, langs={'typescript'}\n  - packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_websocket.py: origins={'orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis', 'websocket-linker-v1'}, langs={'python'}\n  - packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/serve.py: origins={'python-ast-v1', 'websocket-linker-v1'}, langs={'python'}\n\n**What PR #3805 DID fix (derived bugs from the original 3-part claim):**\n1. Wrong language attribution — post-fix, ws-client.ts is language=typescript (was javascript pre-fix), and the .py files are correctly language=python.\n2. Missing stable_id — post-fix, the websocket-linker-v1 file Symbols all carry sha256: stable_ids (were None pre-fix).\n\n**What PR #3805 did NOT fix:**\n3. Duplicates — websocket linker still emits a file-kind Symbol parallel to the language-side / orchestrator-synthesized one. The intended dedup against ctx.symbols isn't catching these cases, OR the websocket linker runs before the orchestrator file-symbol synthesizer, so dedup-against-existing isn't tested at write time.\n\n**Investigation steps (structural-fix protocol):**\n\n1. Read packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/websocket.py around the file-Symbol emission site (was lines 553-556 per the original description).\n2. Determine WHEN websocket linker runs vs orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis: if linker runs first, the dedup against ctx.symbols won't see the synthesized Symbol because it doesn't exist yet.\n3. Two candidate fixes:\n   - (a) Don't emit a file Symbol from websocket linker at all; let the orchestrator synthesizer + the language analyzer cover the canonical file-anchor pseudo-node. Add file-existence-check at edge-creation site instead.\n   - (b) Move the websocket linker's file-Symbol emission to AFTER synthesizer runs, OR emit with the canonical make_file_id shape (which would dedup against existing_ids check in the synthesizer).\n\n**Cross-references:**\n- INV-ronuf (parent, status: pending_validation, kept tagged for now)\n- INV-vaguj (orchestrator synthesizer) — adjacent producer\n- INV-hojus / INV-kokaj (file-canonical kind across languages) — the canonical Symbol shape this linker should produce or defer to\n- INV-dajaf (META: Symbol identity must be honest across pipeline)"  # f56b
    fields: {}  # f56b
- op: discuss  # 9dda
  at: '2026-05-19T08:59:41Z'  # 9dda
  by: agent  # 9dda
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9dda
  clock: 2  # 9dda
  nonce: 9dda  # 9dda
  message: "Fixed by PR #3819 (commit c926c2e5e3, merged to dev).\n\nRoot cause: websocket linker constructed file Symbol ids embedding absolute paths from Path objects yielded by find_js_ts_files / find_python_files. The orchestrator's file-symbol synthesizer + language analyzers emit canonical ids with repo-relative paths (paths normalized in analyze/all_analyzers.py before linkers run). The two id shapes never collided so dedup-against-ctx.symbols silently missed every cross-producer case. Post-linker path normalization at cli.py:7244-7247 fixed Symbol.path but not Symbol.id.\n\nFix: linkers/websocket.py::link_websocket now normalizes pattern.file_path via paths.normalize_path + repo_root prefix-strip (mirroring the orchestrator's exact algorithm byte-equivalently) after pattern collection. All downstream id / path / edge constructions then use repo-relative paths.\n\nVerified by self-analysis dogfood (2026-05-19): 3 -> 0 websocket-origin duplicate file Symbols. Four new tests pin the fix; existing INV-ronuf dedup tests tightened to pass repo-relative existing ids (matching production).\n\nStructural Fix Protocol scope-expansion: same shape found in js_module linker (5 duplicate file Symbols on htrac-frontend .ts paths). Filed as INV-movor.\n\nStatus moved to done."  # 9dda
